# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored; this file is not.
#
# It is read at the two entry points that can need a key — the API's lifespan and
# scripts/run_generation_eval.py — and nowhere else. A real environment variable wins
# over this file, which is how a deployment supplies the key: nothing there reads a
# file at all.
#
# Embedding and retrieval need no keys — embeddings run locally via
# sentence-transformers, against a local Chroma directory.
#
# The access password is REQUIRED and the API will not start without it. /ask returns
# verbatim source text, so unlike the key below this is not optional and has no off
# switch — "off" for generation means serving passages alone, which is a working
# product; "off" here means a reachable URL serving the corpus. Any username works: the
# secret is the password. In a deployment the platform sets this as a real variable.
#
# RAG_ACCESS_PASSWORD=
#
# Generation needs a key, and is optional. Without one the API serves retrieved
# passages and no synthesised answer, which is a working product rather than a
# degraded one — it is exactly what this served before generation existed. That
# is also what keeps the whole test suite runnable with no key.
#
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
